<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine cash wheat steady in good trade.</title>
<headline>Argentine cash wheat steady in good trade.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine wheat was steady to firmer in good volume trade at the Buenos Aires Cereals Exchange, with demand fed by the arrival of ships in port, traders said.</p>
<p>Prices paid to farmers for wheat in Bahia Blanca were unchnaged at $135. May soybeans firmed $3 to $258, with the market still following Wednesday's rises in Chicago. April sunflower seed rose $2 to $203. Cash April maize was unchanged at $101.</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom, +541 318-0655))</p>
